WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.218
Hi, I'm Galloon!

00:00:02.218 --> 00:00:06.549
Timestral reads a stream of numbers and answers with a spread of possible futures.

00:00:06.549 --> 00:00:07.477
Here is how.

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:13.245
Cut the history into patches, read them causally, and let separate forecast

00:00:13.245 --> 00:00:14.903
tokens ask for the future.

00:00:18.692 --> 00:00:20.553
First, the series becomes tokens.

00:00:21.003 --> 00:00:22.995
Cut it into patches of thirty-two steps.

00:00:22.995 --> 00:00:24.419
Each patch is a token.

00:00:24.839 --> 00:00:27.623
Scale each patch by what came before it, never after.

00:00:28.043 --> 00:00:30.101
Squash it, so a huge spike arrives small.

00:00:30.529 --> 00:00:33.498
And flag every missing value, so a gap stays a gap.

00:00:35.092 --> 00:00:37.501
The patches enter a twenty-four layer trunk.

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:40.255
Each one reads only itself and earlier patches.

00:00:40.675 --> 00:00:43.855
Then come forecast tokens, copies of one learned vector.

00:00:43.855 --> 00:00:45.622
They read the whole context.

00:00:45.622 --> 00:00:47.388
The context never reads them.

00:00:47.808 --> 00:00:51.814
A head turns each forecast token into twenty-one quantiles per step, built

00:00:51.814 --> 00:00:53.149
so they cannot cross.

00:00:53.569 --> 00:00:57.098
Every fourth layer also looks across the series' other variables.

00:00:58.692 --> 00:01:00.905
Each quantile is trained with the pinball loss.

00:01:01.325 --> 00:01:03.960
Truth above the forecast costs tau per unit missed.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.604
Truth below costs one minus tau.

00:01:06.604 --> 00:01:09.984
So the forecast settles where a fraction tau falls under it.

00:01:11.717 --> 00:01:15.211
On two shared CPU threads, even the full context took six

00:01:15.211 --> 00:01:16.481
and a half seconds.

00:01:16.481 --> 00:01:18.705
It is only about a thousand tokens.

00:01:19.842 --> 00:01:24.565
The benchmark score, rebuilt from the leaderboard's own files, matches the card exactly.

00:01:27.392 --> 00:01:31.034
So remember: thirty-two thousand steps is only about a thousand tokens.

00:01:31.034 --> 00:01:33.682
That is why it runs on a CPU.

00:01:35.567 --> 00:01:39.648
Patches scaled by the past, forecast tokens that ask for the future,

00:01:39.648 --> 00:01:41.349
and quantiles that cannot cross.

00:01:41.769 --> 00:01:43.905
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:43.905 --> 00:01:44.515
I'm Galloon.

00:01:44.515 --> 00:01:44.820
Bye!
